# crosspost channel credentials
# Copy this file to $CROSSPOST_HOME/.env (default: ~/.crosspost/.env) and fill in
# only the channels you want. Channels with missing credentials are skipped.
#   cp config/.env.example ~/.crosspost/.env && chmod 600 ~/.crosspost/.env
# Run /crosspost:setup for step-by-step guidance per channel.

# ── Common ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Data home override (default: ~/.crosspost)
#CROSSPOST_HOME=

# Shared Chromium CDP port for browser-session channels (Brunch, Naver Blog)
#CROSSPOST_CDP_PORT=9224

# Optional: base URL prepended to canonical post links in channel trailers,
# e.g. your blog. Leave empty to disable trailer links.
#CANONICAL_BASE_URL=https://example.com/insights

# Optional: label used in that trailer (default: "Read the full article")
#CROSSPOST_LINK_TEXT=

# ── LinkedIn (official Posts API) ────────────────────────────────────────────
# Create an app at https://developer.linkedin.com → request w_member_social scope
#LINKEDIN_ACCESS_TOKEN=
#LINKEDIN_PERSON_URN=urn:li:person:XXXXXXXX

# ── Facebook Page (Graph API) ────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Create an app at https://developers.facebook.com → Page access token
# FACEBOOK_APP_ID / FACEBOOK_APP_SECRET are only needed once, to run get-page-token.mjs
# (which then persists FACEBOOK_PAGE_ACCESS_TOKEN below).
#FACEBOOK_APP_ID=
#FACEBOOK_APP_SECRET=
#FACEBOOK_PAGE_ID=
#FACEBOOK_PAGE_ACCESS_TOKEN=
#FACEBOOK_USER_TOKEN=
# Optional: Business Suite keys Insights by the Page's CLASSIC id. On New Pages Experience
# that differs from FACEBOOK_PAGE_ID; set this when fb-reach.mjs says it cannot read the table.
#FACEBOOK_PAGE_ASSET_ID=

# ── Threads (official Graph API) ─────────────────────────────────────────────
# https://developers.facebook.com → Threads use case → user token generator
# Note: user tokens expire ~60 days; re-issue when you see 401s.
#THREADS_ACCESS_TOKEN=
#THREADS_USER_ID=
# Optional: Meta app secret, shared with Facebook when both products live under the same
# app. facebook/get-page-token.mjs falls back to this if FACEBOOK_APP_SECRET is unset.
#THREADS_APP_SECRET=

# ── X / Twitter (official API v2, OAuth 1.0a user context) ───────────────────
# https://developer.x.com → create app → keys & tokens
#X_API_KEY=
#X_API_SECRET=
#X_ACCESS_TOKEN=
#X_ACCESS_SECRET=

# ── Remember Connect (unofficial, experimental) ──────────────────────────────
# Bearer token captured from a logged-in connect.rememberapp.co.kr session.
# Unofficial private API — may break at any time; use at your own risk.
#REMEMBER_TOKEN=
# Your Remember profile id, used by remember-stats.mjs to fetch your own posts
# (list_by_author). Find it in a logged-in browser's network tab: any
# connect-api.rememberapp.co.kr request body carries it as `open_profile_id`.
#REMEMBER_PROFILE_ID=

# ── Brunch (browser session via CDP — Korean platform, no official API) ──────
# Requires one-time manual Kakao login in the persistent browser profile.
#BRUNCH_COOKIE=
# Optional: Kakao ID/password for unattended session self-heal when the SSO cookie
# itself expires (~monthly). Falls back to human re-login in the browser if unset
# or if Kakao shows a 2FA/device-approval wall.
#KAKAO_ID=
#KAKAO_PW=

# ── Naver Blog (browser session via CDP — no official write API) ─────────────
# Requires one-time manual Naver login in the persistent browser profile.
#NAVER_BLOG_ID=

# ── Instagram (official Graph API; Business/Creator account) ─────────────────
# Meta fetches image/video media from this public HTTPS base URL.
#IG_USER_ID=
#IG_ACCESS_TOKEN=
#CROSSPOST_MEDIA_BASE_URL=https://media.example.com/crosspost

# ── Follow tools (optional — only for `/publish follow` and `/publish list`) ──
# Reading followers/likers and following back is separate from publishing, and each
# channel needs one more identifier or session than publishing does. Leave a line
# unset and that channel simply sits out the follow/list run.
#
# Automated following is against most platforms' terms of service. LinkedIn and the
# Meta channels police it hardest; the scripts default to a small cap, a long delay,
# and a loud warning on any non-dry run. Preview with --dry-run first.

# Brunch: your own userId (the `@@<id>` in brunch.co.kr subscription URLs). Without it
# the tool asks the browser once and prints the value to put here.
#BRUNCH_USER_ID=
# Instagram: the account handle whose followers/likers are read. This is NOT IG_USER_ID
# (that one is the Graph publishing id, a different namespace).
#IG_USERNAME=
# Facebook: your PERSONAL profile slug or numeric id — a Page cannot follow people.
# Public followers exist only when the profile has professional mode enabled.
#FACEBOOK_PROFILE=
# LinkedIn: li_at + JSESSIONID captured from a logged-in browser. Kept separate from
# LINKEDIN_COOKIE, which holds li_at alone for the stats reader. Captured automatically
# from the CDP browser when unset.
#LINKEDIN_FOLLOW_COOKIE=
# Threads: override the handle instead of deriving it from the logged-in session.
#THREADS_HANDLE=
